Limitations with free Ultimate Member and Meta Box:
- Ultimate Member (free):
  - No built-in front-end post forms. You must hand-roll forms/handlers (as above) or use UM Pro/add-ons.
  - Limited access control granularity for custom post capabilities; mapping WP caps to UM roles may require custom code or paid extensions.
  - UM templates/hooks may change across versions; custom tabs rely on action/filter names that can differ with major updates.
- Meta Box (free):
  - Free core registers/saves fields in admin; front-end form rendering is not included without Meta Box extensions (e.g., MB Frontend Submission – paid).
  - Some complex field types (repeaters, groups, file/image advanced) need premium extensions for easy front-end handling; otherwise you must manually build inputs and save post meta (as in this example).

Security and best practices:
- Nonces and capability checks: Already included; keep them on every action (create/update/delete). Also validate author ownership when editing/deleting.
- Capability model: Define custom capabilities on the CPT (capability_type + map_meta_cap) and grant via UM roles to avoid overpermission (e.g., avoid giving edit_others_posts).
- Sanitization/escaping: Sanitize on input, escape on output (demonstrated). For rich text, restrict allowed HTML with wp_kses_post.
- File uploads: Enforce MIME and size checks server-side; consider using a dedicated uploads directory and additional scans if public submissions are allowed.
- Moderation workflow: Use pending for create/update and notify admins to review; expose status to users.
- Rate limiting/spam: Consider throttling submissions per user/IP or require email-verified/approved UM roles.
- Separate plugin vs theme: Prefer a small mu-plugin or site-specific plugin (like this) instead of theme functions.php for portability and to survive theme switches.

Alternatives and enhancements:
- Use Meta Box Frontend Submission (paid) to generate and handle front-end forms automatically, then embed forms in the UM tab via shortcode do_shortcode within the tab renderer.
- Use dedicated front-end post plugins (e.g., ACF Frontend, WP User Frontend, Gravity Forms + GF Post Creation, Formidable, Ninja Forms) and integrate into UM tabs with shortcodes or hooks.
- For listing multiple Artiste posts per user, replace one-per-user logic with a user-scoped query + pagination and add create-new form separate from edit form.
- If you need revision history or preview, leverage WP revisions and show preview links; restrict publishes to editors.
- For performance/UX, use AJAX endpoints (wp_ajax_) to handle save/delete and return JSON; progressively enhance with JS while keeping non-JS fallback.

Information needed from you to tailor the code precisely:
- Exact CPT slug/labels and whether it already exists (and its capability settings).
- The Meta Box field IDs, types, and any special validation rules.
- Desired statuses/workflow (draft/pending/publish) and moderation policy.
- Which UM roles should be allowed to manage Artiste.
- Whether users may have multiple Artistes or only one.
- Required media constraints (types, size, dimensions) and thumbnails/sizes to display.
- Any specific layout/design requirements for the UM tab.

Below is a complete, self-contained MATLAB implementation of a 2-D source panel method with the requested functionality and structure. It:

- Reads panel points from a user-specified text file (same format as before: two columns x y, ordered around the body).
- Prompts for free-stream speed U∞ and angle of attack α (degrees).
- Builds constant-strength source panels, solves for panel strengths to satisfy no-penetration boundary conditions.
- Computes surface Cp and compares it to the analytic solution for a circle in uniform flow at AoA α when applicable; otherwise, prints a clear warning and reports Cp without comparison.
- Estimates circulation from tangential velocities and computes Cl via Kutta–Joukowski; compares to Cl = 2π·α (radians) if geometry is a circle; otherwise, prints a clear warning.
- Includes basic error handling and degenerate-panel protection.
- Uses only base MATLAB (no toolboxes).
- Organized into a main script with helper functions.

Save the file as source_panel_2D_main.m and run. The script will prompt for the input file, U∞, and α.

-------------------- FILE: source_panel_2D_main.m --------------------
function source_panel_2D_main()
% SOURCE_PANEL_2D_MAIN
% 2-D constant-strength source panel method.
% - Reads geometry from user-specified text file: two columns [x y]
% - Prompts for free-stream speed Uinf and angle of attack alpha (deg)
% - Solves for source strengths enforcing no-penetration
% - Computes surface pressure coefficient Cp
% - Computes lift coefficient Cl via Kutta–Joukowski from circulation
% - If the geometry is a circle, compares Cp and Cl to analytical results
% - Provides basic error handling and clean console outputs
%
% No external toolboxes required.

clc;
fprintf('=== 2-D Source Panel Method (Constant Strength) ===\n');

% 1) Read geometry
[x, y] = readGeometryFromFilePrompt();
if isempty(x); return; end

% 2) Prompt flow conditions
[Uinf, alpha_deg] = promptFlowConditions();
if isempty(Uinf); return; end
alpha = deg2rad(alpha_deg); % radians

% 3) Build panels
geom = buildPanels(x, y);
if isempty(geom); return; end

% 4) Assemble influence matrix and RHS
[A, rhs] = buildSystem(geom, Uinf, alpha);

% 5) Solve for source strengths (sigma)
sigma = solveSystem(A, rhs);

% 6) Compute surface velocities and Cp
[Cp, Vt] = computeCp(geom, sigma, Uinf, alpha);

% 7) Estimate circulation and lift coefficient
[circ, Cl] = computeCirculationAndCl(geom, Vt, Uinf);

% 8) Detect circle and, if applicable, produce analytical comparisons
isCircle = detectCircle(geom);
if isCircle
    % Estimate circle parameters from geometry
    [xc, yc, R] = fitCircleLeastSquares(geom.xc, geom.yc);
    if ~isnan(R) && R > 0
        [Cp_ana, s_pan] = analyticCpCircle(geom, Uinf, alpha, [xc yc R]);
        Cl_ana = 2*pi*alpha; % small-angle in radians

        % Console outputs
        fprintf('\nCircle detected (center ≈ [%.5g, %.5g], R ≈ %.5g).\n', xc, yc, R);
        fprintf('Computed Cl = %.6f; Analytical Cl = 2*pi*alpha = %.6f\n', Cl, Cl_ana);

        % Plot Cp comparison
        plotCpComparison(geom, Cp, Cp_ana, s_pan);

    else
        warnNoCircle();
        plotCpBasic(geom, Cp);
    end
else
    warnNoCircle();
    plotCpBasic(geom, Cp);
end

% 9) Plot geometry and panel normals
plotGeometry(geom);

% 10) Final console summary
fprintf('\n=== Summary ===\n');
fprintf('Uinf = %.6g, alpha = %.6g deg\n', Uinf, alpha_deg);
fprintf('Panels: %d\n', geom.N);
fprintf('Total circulation Γ = %.6g\n', circ);
fprintf('Lift coefficient Cl = %.6f\n', Cl);
fprintf('Note: For non-circular geometry, Cp and Cl are reported without analytical comparison.\n');

end

% ========================= Helper Functions =========================

function [x, y] = readGeometryFromFilePrompt()
% readGeometryFromFilePrompt
% Prompts user for a geometry file path and reads points [x y].
% Requirements: two columns, at least 3 points, closed polygon or will be auto-closed.
% Returns:
%   x, y: column vectors of node coordinates
% On failure, returns empty arrays.

x = []; y = [];

try
    file = input('Enter path to geometry file (two columns x y): ', 's');
    if isempty(file)
        error('No file path entered.');
    end
    if ~isfile(file)
        error('File not found: %s', file);
    end
    data = readmatrix(file);
    if ~isnumeric(data) || size(data,2) < 2
        error('File must contain at least two numeric columns [x y].');
    end
    data = data(:,1:2);
    if any(~isfinite(data), 'all')
        error('File contains non-finite entries.');
    end
    if size(data,1) < 3
        error('At least 3 points are required.');
    end
    x = data(:,1); y = data(:,2);

    % Ensure column vectors
    x = x(:); y = y(:);

    % Check closure; if not closed, append first point at end
    if norm([x(1)-x(end), y(1)-y(end)]) > 1e-12
        x = [x; x(1)];
        y = [y; y(1)];
        fprintf('Note: Geometry was not closed. First point appended to close polygon.\n');
    end

catch ME
    fprintf(2, 'Error reading geometry: %s\n', ME.message);
    x = []; y = [];
end
end

function [Uinf, alpha_deg] = promptFlowConditions()
% promptFlowConditions
% Prompts user for Uinf and alpha (deg).
% Returns empty if invalid.

Uinf = []; alpha_deg = [];
try
    Uinf = str2double(input('Enter free-stream speed Uinf (>0): ', 's'));
    alpha_deg = str2double(input('Enter angle of attack alpha (deg): ', 's'));
    if ~isfinite(Uinf) || Uinf <= 0
        error('Uinf must be a positive number.');
    end
    if ~isfinite(alpha_deg)
        error('alpha must be a numeric value (degrees).');
    end
catch ME
    fprintf(2, 'Invalid input: %s\n', ME.message);
    Uinf = []; alpha_deg = [];
end
end

function geom = buildPanels(x, y)
% buildPanels
% Builds panel data structure from node coordinates.
% Inputs:
%   x, y: node coordinates (closed polygon; last equals first)
% Outputs:
%   geom: struct with fields:
%     N, x, y, xa, ya, xb, yb, xc, yc, S, theta, nx, ny, tx, ty

geom = struct();
try
    % Remove duplicate trailing nodes beyond closure if any
    % Keep only one closure at end equal to first
    if norm([x(1)-x(end), y(1)-y(end)]) > 1e-12
        error('Polygon must be closed. Last point must equal first.');
    end
    % Remove consecutive duplicate points
    keep = [true; sqrt(diff(x).^2 + diff(y).^2) > 1e-14];
    x = x(keep); y = y(keep);
    % Ensure closure after removing duplicates
    if norm([x(1)-x(end), y(1)-y(end)]) > 1e-12
        x = [x; x(1)]; y = [y; y(1)];
    end

    N = length(x)-1; % number of panels
    if N < 2
        error('Insufficient distinct points to form panels.');
    end

    xa = x(1:N);     ya = y(1:N);
    xb = x(2:N+1);   yb = y(2:N+1);

    % Panel geometry
    dx = xb - xa; dy = yb - ya;
    S  = sqrt(dx.^2 + dy.^2);

    % Handle degenerate (zero-length) panels
    bad = S < 1e-12;
    if any(bad)
        nbad = sum(bad);
        fprintf(2, 'Warning: %d degenerate panels detected and removed.\n', nbad);
        xa = xa(~bad); ya = ya(~bad);
        xb = xb(~bad); yb = yb(~bad);
        dx = xb - xa;  dy = yb - ya;
        S  = sqrt(dx.^2 + dy.^2);
    end

    N = numel(S);
    if N < 2
        error('Not enough valid panels after removing degenerates.');
    end

    theta = atan2(dy, dx);        % panel orientation (x-axis -> panel)
    tx = cos(theta); ty = sin(theta); % unit tangents
    nx = -sin(theta); ny = cos(theta); % outward normals (left-hand side)

    % Collocation points (midpoints)
    xc = 0.5*(xa + xb);
    yc = 0.5*(ya + yb);

    geom.N = N;
    geom.x = x; geom.y = y;
    geom.xa = xa; geom.ya = ya; geom.xb = xb; geom.yb = yb;
    geom.xc = xc; geom.yc = yc; geom.S = S;
    geom.theta = theta; geom.nx = nx; geom.ny = ny;
    geom.tx = tx; geom.ty = ty;

catch ME
    fprintf(2, 'Error building panels: %s\n', ME.message);
    geom = [];
end
end

function [A, rhs] = buildSystem(geom, Uinf, alpha)
% buildSystem
% Assembles the linear system A*sigma = rhs for no-penetration.
% Influence: normal velocity at collocation i due to unit source on panel j.
% Free-stream contribution: -Uinf*(cos(alpha)*nxi + sin(alpha)*nyi)
% Inputs:
%   geom, Uinf, alpha
% Outputs:
%   A [N x N], rhs [N x 1]

N = geom.N;
A = zeros(N,N);
rhs = zeros(N,1);

% Loop over panels i (collocation) and j (source panels)
for i = 1:N
    for j = 1:N
        A(i,j) = normalInfluence(geom, i, j);
    end
    % RHS: - V_inf · n_i
    rhs(i) = -Uinf*(cos(alpha)*geom.nx(i) + sin(alpha)*geom.ny(i));
end

% Regularization: none normally needed; matrix should be well-conditioned
end

function aij = normalInfluence(geom, i, j)
% normalInfluence
% Computes normal velocity at collocation point i due to unit-strength
% source distributed uniformly over panel j.
% Uses panel-local coordinates analytic integrals (standard source panel).
% Returns scalar aij.

% Vector from panel j's start to end
xj1 = geom.xa(j); yj1 = geom.ya(j);
xj2 = geom.xb(j); yj2 = geom.yb(j);
Sj  = geom.S(j);
theta = geom.theta(j);
ct = cos(theta); st = sin(theta);

% Collocation point i in global
xi = geom.xc(i); yi = geom.yc(i);

% Transform collocation point to panel-j local frame
xip =  (xi - xj1)*ct + (yi - yj1)*st;  % along panel
yip = -(xi - xj1)*st + (yi - yj1)*ct;  % normal to panel (positive is panel's outward normal)

% Avoid singularities: if very close to panel line, slightly offset
epsy = 0; % analytic formulas handle off-line; if exactly zero, add tiny offset
if abs(yip) < 1e-14
    yip = sign(yip + 1e-16)*1e-14;
end

% Endpoints in local x
xA = 0; xB = Sj;

% Standard integrals for unit source panel (see e.g., Hess & Smith)
% Velocity components in panel-local frame at (xip, yip):
% u_local (along x), v_local (normal y) from a unit source strength per unit length
% Influence on normal velocity at collocation i is v_local rotated to global n_i.
% But we need normal component at i projected to i's normal. Easier approach:
% Compute induced velocity vector in global at (xi,yi), then dot with n_i.

% Local induced velocities from a unit-strength source panel (per unit length)
% u_loc = (1/(2*pi)) * [atan2((xB - xip), yip) - atan2((xA - xip), yip)]
% v_loc = (-1/(4*pi)) * ln( ((xB - xip)^2 + yip^2) / ((xA - xip)^2 + yip^2) )
% Reference: standard constant-strength source panel formulas.

phi1 = atan2((xB - xip), yip);
phi0 = atan2((xA - xip), yip);
u_loc = (1/(2*pi)) * (phi1 - phi0);

r1sq = (xB - xip)^2 + yip^2;
r0sq = (xA - xip)^2 + yip^2;
% Guard against log of non-positive due to round-off
r1sq = max(r1sq, 1e-30);
r0sq = max(r0sq, 1e-30);
v_loc = (-1/(4*pi)) * log(r1sq / r0sq);

% Rotate local velocities to global
ux =  u_loc*ct - v_loc*st;
uy =  u_loc*st + v_loc*ct;

% Project to normal of collocation panel i
aij = ux*geom.nx(i) + uy*geom.ny(i);

% Self-influence special case i==j:
% The above analytic formula is valid and finite for yip ≠ 0.
% In the limit yip->0, the normal influence equals 0.5 (for source panels).
% We can enforce this for numerical robustness when i==j.
if i == j
    aij = 0.5;
end
end

function sigma = solveSystem(A, rhs)
% solveSystem
% Solves A*sigma = rhs with basic checks.

sigma = zeros(size(rhs));
try
    % Check conditioning lightly
    if rcond(A) < 1e-12
        fprintf(2, 'Warning: System matrix is poorly conditioned (rcond=%.3e).\n', rcond(A));
    end
    sigma = A\rhs;
catch ME
    fprintf(2, 'Error solving linear system: %s\n', ME.message);
    sigma = [];
end
end

function [Cp, Vt] = computeCp(geom, sigma, Uinf, alpha)
% computeCp
% Computes tangential velocity and Cp at panel collocation points.
% For a source-only body in uniform flow, the tangential component comes from
% the superposition of:
%   - free-stream projected on tangential direction
%   - induced velocity from all source panels, projected tangentially
% Inputs:
%   geom, sigma, Uinf, alpha
% Outputs:
%   Cp [N x 1], Vt [N x 1] tangential velocity at each panel collocation

N = geom.N;
Vt = zeros(N,1);

% Free-stream contribution to tangential velocity
Vt = Uinf*(cos(alpha)*geom.tx + sin(alpha)*geom.ty);

% Add induced from all panels
for i = 1:N
    % Induced velocity vector from each panel j at collocation i
    Vi = [0;0];
    for j = 1:N
        [ux, uy] = inducedVelocityUnitSource(geom, i, j);
        Vi = Vi + sigma(j)*[ux; uy];
    end
    % Tangential projection
    Vt(i) = (Vi(1)*geom.tx(i) + Vi(2)*geom.ty(i)) + Uinf*(cos(alpha)*geom.tx(i) + sin(alpha)*geom.ty(i));
end

Cp = 1 - (Vt./Uinf).^2;
end

function [ux, uy] = inducedVelocityUnitSource(geom, i, j)
% inducedVelocityUnitSource
% Returns induced velocity components (ux, uy) at collocation i
% due to a unit-strength source panel j.

% Panel j geometry
xj1 = geom.xa(j); yj1 = geom.ya(j);
Sj  = geom.S(j);
theta = geom.theta(j);
ct = cos(theta); st = sin(theta);

% Collocation point i
xi = geom.xc(i); yi = geom.yc(i);

% Transform to panel-local frame
xip =  (xi - xj1)*ct + (yi - yj1)*st;
yip = -(xi - xj1)*st + (yi - yj1)*ct;

% Avoid exact alignment for numerical safety
if abs(yip) < 1e-14
    yip = sign(yip + 1e-16)*1e-14;
end
xA = 0; xB = Sj;

phi1 = atan2((xB - xip), yip);
phi0 = atan2((xA - xip), yip);
u_loc = (1/(2*pi)) * (phi1 - phi0);

r1sq = (xB - xip)^2 + yip^2;
r0sq = (xA - xip)^2 + yip^2;
r1sq = max(r1sq, 1e-30);
r0sq = max(r0sq, 1e-30);
v_loc = (-1/(4*pi)) * log(r1sq / r0sq);

% Rotate to global
ux =  u_loc*ct - v_loc*st;
uy =  u_loc*st + v_loc*ct;
end

function [circ, Cl] = computeCirculationAndCl(geom, Vt, Uinf)
% computeCirculationAndCl
% Estimates total circulation by integrating tangential velocity along the body:
%   Γ ≈ sum_i Vt(i) * ds_i (right-hand rule; positive CCW)
% Then lift per unit span L' = rho * Uinf * Γ, so Cl = L'/(0.5*rho*Uinf^2*c_ref).
% For 2D coefficient, we use a reference length c_ref = chord-like measure.
% Here we adopt c_ref = max(x)-min(x) (bounding-box chord).
%
% Inputs:
%   geom, Vt, Uinf
% Outputs:
%   circ (scalar), Cl (scalar)

% Circulation (sign convention: CCW positive)
circ = sum(Vt .* geom.S); % integral along panel midpoints approximation

% Reference length: projected chord in x
c_ref = max(geom.x) - min(geom.x);
if c_ref <= 0
    % Fallback to perimeter/(pi) as a scale
    c_ref = sum(geom.S)/pi;
end

% Cl = 2*Gamma / (Uinf * c_ref)
Cl = 2 * circ / (Uinf * c_ref);
end

function isCirc = detectCircle(geom)
% detectCircle
% Heuristic: Fit a circle to panel midpoints and check radial variance
% relative to mean radius.
% Returns true if geometry appears circular.

[xc, yc, R] = fitCircleLeastSquares(geom.xc, geom.yc);
if isnan(R) || R <= 0
    isCirc = false;
    return;
end
r = hypot(geom.xc - xc, geom.yc - yc);
err = std(r)/mean(r);
isCirc = err < 0.01; % 1% relative std threshold
end

function [xc, yc, R] = fitCircleLeastSquares(x, y)
% fitCircleLeastSquares
% Algebraic circle fit (Kasa method).
% Returns NaN on failure.

xc = NaN; yc = NaN; R = NaN;
x = x(:); y = y(:);
if numel(x) < 3
    return;
end
A = [2*x, 2*y, ones(size(x))];
b = x.^2 + y.^2;
if rank(A) < 3
    return;
end
p = A\b;
xc = p(1); yc = p(2);
R = sqrt(max(p(3) + xc^2 + yc^2, 0));
end

function [Cp_ana, s_pan] = analyticCpCircle(geom, Uinf, alpha, circle)
% analyticCpCircle
% Analytical Cp on a circle in uniform flow at AoA alpha:
% V_theta = 2*Uinf*sin(theta - alpha), theta measured from +x axis from center
% Cp = 1 - (V/Uinf)^2 = 1 - 4*sin^2(theta - alpha)
% Returns Cp at panel midpoints ordered by arc-length s_pan.

xc = circle(1); yc = circle(2);
% Radius from fit (not strictly needed except for s mapping)
R = mean(hypot(geom.xc - xc, geom.yc - yc));

theta = atan2(geom.yc - yc, geom.xc - xc); % angle of midpoint from center
Cp_ana = 1 - 4*sin(theta - alpha).^2;

% Arc-length from first panel midpoint, monotonically increasing
% Sort by theta for smooth plotting
[theta_sorted, idx] = sort(unwrap(theta));
Cp_ana = Cp_ana(idx);
% Compute cumulative arc-length along sorted points
s_pan = [0; cumsum(hypot(diff(geom.xc(idx)), diff(geom.yc(idx))))];
% Reorder Cp_ana back to original order for return?
% We keep Cp_ana aligned with sorted s_pan for comparison plotting only.
% The caller uses this pair for plotting.
end

function warnNoCircle()
fprintf(2, '\nWarning: Input geometry is not detected as a circle. ');
fprintf(2, 'Analytical Cp/Cl comparisons are skipped.\n');
end

function plotCpComparison(geom, Cp_num, Cp_ana_sorted, s_pan)
% plotCpComparison
% Plots numerical Cp vs arc-length and overlays analytical Cp for circle.
% Numerical Cp is plotted against body arc-length from first panel.

figure('Name','Cp Comparison','Color','w');
% Numerical Cp: compute s along panel midpoints in original order
s_num = [0; cumsum(geom.S(1:end-1))];
plot(s_num, Cp_num, 'o-', 'LineWidth', 1.5, 'DisplayName','Numerical Cp');
hold on;
plot(s_pan, Cp_ana_sorted, 'r-', 'LineWidth', 1.5, 'DisplayName','Analytical Cp (circle)');
set(gca, 'YDir','reverse'); % conventional Cp plotting
xlabel('Arc length s');
ylabel('Cp');
legend('Location','best');
grid on;
title('Surface Pressure Coefficient Cp');
hold off;
end

function plotCpBasic(geom, Cp)
% plotCpBasic
% Plots Cp vs arc length only (no analytical comparison).

figure('Name','Cp','Color','w');
s = [0; cumsum(geom.S(1:end-1))];
plot(s, Cp, 'o-', 'LineWidth', 1.5);
set(gca, 'YDir','reverse');
xlabel('Arc length s');
ylabel('Cp');
grid on;
title('Surface Pressure Coefficient Cp (numerical)');
end

function plotGeometry(geom)
% plotGeometry
% Plots body outline, panel midpoints, and normals.

figure('Name','Geometry','Color','w');
plot(geom.x, geom.y, 'k-', 'LineWidth', 1.5); hold on;
plot(geom.xc, geom.yc, 'bo', 'MarkerSize', 4, 'DisplayName','Midpoints');
% Plot normals
scale = 0.2 * max(geom.S);
quiver(geom.xc, geom.yc, geom.nx*scale, geom.ny*scale, 0, 'r', 'LineWidth', 1.0, 'DisplayName','Normals');
axis equal; grid on;
xlabel('x'); ylabel('y');
title(sprintf('Geometry and Panel Normals (N = %d)', geom.N));
legend('Location','best');
hold off;
end

