//! Minimal 'sysx' init and controller for Devuan without systemd/sysvinit.
//!
//! - Single binary with two roles:
//!   * "init" path when running as PID 1 (or via `sysx init`): bring up mounts, network,
//!     and supervise a getty on tty1.
//!   * "ctl" path when not PID 1 (or via `sysx ctl`): control/list/logs via a Unix socket.
//!
//! - No systemd, no dbus, no X, no external daemons. Uses /sbin/fsck, /bin/mount,
//!   /sbin/ip, /sbin/udhcpc, and /sbin/agetty only if present.
//!
//! - Tasks:
//!   * mounts      -> performs fsck and mounts filesystems
//!   * network     -> brings up loopback and DHCP on first non-loopback iface
//!   * getty@tty1  -> agetty on tty1
//!
//! - Supervision:
//!   * Restart policy: Never, OnFailure, Always
//!   * Exponential backoff up to 30s
//!   * Line-oriented stdout/err logged to /var/log/sysx/<task>.log
//!
//! - Signals:
//!   * SIGCHLD: reap children and update task states
//!   * SIGTERM/SIGINT (init role): initiate graceful shutdown: stop tasks, sync,
//!     remount ro, poweroff via reboot(RB_POWER_OFF).
//!
//! Build: cargo build --release (Rust 1.74+)

