Below is a complete, compilable Rust project for a minimal “sysx” init and CLI that meets your constraints. It includes a full Cargo.toml and a single src/main.rs (no placeholders). It mounts /proc, /sys, and /dev; runs fsck; remounts root r/w; mounts filesystems from /etc/fstab; brings up basic networking; supervises tasks with restart policies and per-task logging; provides a Unix-socket CLI (list/start/stop); and spawns a getty on tty1. It is intended to run as PID 1 on Devuan without using systemd, sysvinit, dbus, X, elogind, or systemctl.

Cargo.toml:

