Unity material/keyword setup
- Create two Materials:
  - Hidden/URP/ContactBand/LinearizeDepth (URP) or Hidden/HDRP/ContactBand/CopyLinearDepth (HDRP).
  - Hidden/URP/ContactBand/Composite or Hidden/HDRP/ContactBand/Composite.
- No special keywords required. Set _BandWidth on the composite material in meters (e.g., 0.25).
- In URP Renderer, add the ContactBandURPFeature, assign Terrain layer and Mountain layer.
- Ensure Depth Texture is enabled in URP/HDRP asset. MSAA disabled.

Notes on linear depth
- We store linear eye depth in meters in RFloat (GraphicsFormat.R32_SFloat).
- Linearization used: d = near * far / lerp(far, near, z01). Works for standard Unity projection (reversed Z off in 2021.3 URP/HDRP 12 default). If reversed Z is enabled, use appropriate formula; with MSAA off and defaults this form is correct.

Unreal Engine 5.3 — Post Process Material and setup

Material: M_ContactBandComposite
- Domain: Surface
- Material Domain: Post Process
- Blendable Location: Before Tonemapping
- Shading Model: Unlit
- Output: Emissive Color = result color, Opacity = 1.

External inputs (TextureObjects/TextureSamples):
- T_TerrainColor: RenderTarget2D RGBA8 or RGBA16F
- T_MountainColor: RenderTarget2D RGBA8 or RGBA16F
- T_TerrainDepthLinear: RenderTarget2D R32Float
- T_MountainDepthLinear: RenderTarget2D R32Float
- Samplers: Clamp, Point for depth; Clamp, Linear for color
- Scalar parameter: BandWidthMeters (Default 0.25)

Linearizing scene depth (for occlusion clamp checks):
- SceneDepth node returns device depth in 0..1. Convert to linear meters:
  - Custom node HLSL (Depth01ToLinear): return Near * Far / lerp(Far, Near, x);
  - Near, Far from CameraParameters (View.WorldToMeters, View.NearPlane, View.FarPlane). In UE5, Far is very large; clamp to your capture far plane.

Material graph node list and connections
- Parameters:
  - ScalarParameter BandWidthMeters -> w
  - TextureObject T_TerrainColor, T_MountainColor
  - TextureObject T_TerrainDepthLinear (R32F), T_MountainDepthLinear (R32F)
- TextureSample nodes:
  - Sample T_TerrainColor (linear sampler) -> cT (RGB)
  - Sample T_MountainColor (linear sampler) -> cM (RGB)
  - Sample T_TerrainDepthLinear (point sampler) -> dT
  - Sample T_MountainDepthLinear (point sampler) -> dM
- Compute:
  - dCam = Min(dT, dM)
  - s = dM - dT
  - t = saturate(0.5 + 0.5 * s / w)
  - inside = Step(abs(s), w - 1e-6) [use Custom HLSL node StepInsideBand: return (abs(x) <= y) ? 1.0 : 0.0;]
  - strict = (dT <= dM) ? cT : cM [Use If node: A=dT<=dM, A>=B? cT : cM]
  - bandMix = Lerp(cM, cT, t)
  - tBehind = (dT - dCam) > w && abs(dM - dCam) <= 1e-6
  - mBehind = (dM - dCam) > w && abs(dT - dCam) <= 1e-6
  - mixed = inside ? bandMix : strict
  - If tBehind: mixed = cM; If mBehind: mixed = cT
- Outputs:
  - Emissive Color = mixed
  - Opacity = 1

UE5 Custom node snippets
- StepInsideBand(x, w):
float StepInsideBand(float x, float w) { return (abs(x) <= (w - 1e-6)) ? 1.0 : 0.0; }
- Depth01ToLinear(z01, Near, Far):
float Depth01ToLinear(float z01, float Near, float Far) { return Near * Far / lerp(Far, Near, z01); }

Producing the two color and two depth render targets
- Create two SceneCapture2D actors:
  - SC_Terrain: CaptureSource = Final Color (LDR with PostProcess disabled) or BaseColor in LDR if you want pure albedo.
  - SC_Mountain: same.
  - Each writes to:
    - RT_TerrainColor: Format RGBA8 or RGBA16f.
    - RT_TerrainDepth: Format RTF R32f (RFloat).
  - Set FOV/Projection/Clip planes identical to main camera (Near/Far).
  - Use ShowOnlyList to isolate:
    - SC_Terrain -> ShowOnlyActors or ShowOnlyComponents contains only terrain meshes.
    - SC_Mountain -> ShowOnlyActors or ShowOnlyComponents contains only mountain meshes.
  - Depth: For each SceneCapture, also enable CaptureSource = SceneDepth in a second component or use a SceneCapture2D with "CaptureEveryFrame" and add a second capture or a Composure/RenderTarget setup to output depth to RTM R32f using a custom material applied via PostProcessMaterial on the capture.
- Alternatively, use CustomDepth/Stencil:
  - Enable Project Settings -> Rendering -> Postprocessing -> Custom Depth-Stencil Pass = Enabled with Stencil.
  - Tag terrain meshes Stencil=1, mountain meshes Stencil=2; render two capture passes filtering by Stencil to emit color and a custom post-process on the capture material to write SceneDepth (converted to linear meters) into R32f RTs.

UE5 Post Process material binding
- Create TextureParameter2D nodes: TerrainColor, MountainColor, TerrainDepthLinear, MountainDepthLinear.
- Assign the four render targets from your SceneCaptures to these parameters in a Post Process Volume or at runtime via Blueprint/Code.
- Create a Post Process Volume (Unbound) and add M_ContactBandComposite in Blendables, placed Before Tonemapping.

Exact HLSL for the core in UE material (single Custom node returning float3 color)
Inputs: cT (float3), cM (float3), dT (float), dM (float), w (float)
float3 ContactBand(float3 cT, float3 cM, float dT, float dM, float w)
{
    float dCam = min(dT, dM);
    float s = dM - dT;
    float t = saturate(0.5 + 0.5 * s / max(w, 1e-6));
    float inside = (abs(s) <= (w - 1e-6)) ? 1.0 : 0.0;
    float3 strict = (dT <= dM) ? cT : cM;
    float3 bandMix = lerp(cM, cT, t);
    float3 mixed = inside > 0.5 ? bandMix : strict;

    bool tBehind = ((dT - dCam) > w) && (abs(dM - dCam) <= 1e-6);
    bool mBehind = ((dM - dCam) > w) && (abs(dT - dCam) <= 1e-6);
    if (tBehind) mixed = cM;
    if (mBehind) mixed = cT;
    return mixed;
}

UE linear depth formula (for your depth RTs)
- When writing depth RTs from a SceneCapture material: d = Near * Far / lerp(Far, Near, SceneDepth);
- Store to R32f.

Important formats
- Depth RTs: R32 Float (RFloat).
- Color RTs: RGBA8 or RGBA16F (disable sRGB on intermediate RTs; the post-process reads linear).
- Unity: GraphicsFormat.R32_SFloat for linear depths.

Notes and caveats
- The provided Unity URP/HDRP snippets assume you bind separate terrain/mountain color RTs to _TerrainColor/_MountainColor. The feature shows where to set them; in your project, render those via additional cameras or layer-only cameras into color RTs and assign them before the composite.
- Make sure all cameras share identical projection (near/far/FOV), and MSAA is off, for texel-perfect alignment.
- If you use reversed Z or non-standard projection, adjust the linearization accordingly.

//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
//|                                           EMA_RSI_ATR_Manager.mq5 |
//|     EMA Cross + RSI + ATR with robust risk & margin management    |
//|     One-position-per-symbol, spread/session filters, trailing SL  |
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
#property strict
#property copyright ""
#property version   "1.00"
#property description "EMA Cross + RSI + ATR strategy with complete trade management, robust margin/risk logic, and filters."

#include <Trade/Trade.mqh>
CTrade trade;

//========================
// Inputs: Strategy & Risk
//========================
input ENUM_TIMEFRAMES InpTimeframe      = PERIOD_M5;    // Signal timeframe
input int             InpFastEMA        = 21;           // Fast EMA period
input int             InpSlowEMA        = 55;           // Slow EMA period
input int             InpRSIPeriod      = 14;           // RSI period
input double          InpRSI_Buy        = 55.0;         // RSI threshold for buys
input double          InpRSI_Sell       = 45.0;         // RSI threshold for sells
input int             InpATRPeriod      = 14;           // ATR period
input double          InpATR_SL_Mult    = 1.5;          // SL = ATR * this multiplier
input double          InpATR_TrailMult  = 1.0;          // Trailing distance = ATR * this multiplier
input double          InpRR             = 2.0;          // Reward:Risk ratio
input double          InpATR_MinFilter  = 0.0;          // Minimum ATR filter (price units); set 0 to disable

//========================
// Inputs: Risk Management
//========================
input double          InpRiskPerTradePct          = 0.5;    // Percent of equity risked per trade
input double          InpMaxFreeMarginUsagePct     = 10.0;   // Cap: single trade uses <= this % of free margin
input double          InpMinMarginLevelPct         = 500.0;  // Do not open if margin level below this (%), ignore if 0 or if AccountInfo returns 0
input ulong           InpMagicNumber               = 987654321; // Magic number

//========================
// Inputs: Execution & Filters
//========================
input int             InpSlippagePoints            = 20;     // Max deviation (points)
input int             InpMaxSpreadPoints           = 30;     // Max spread (points) to allow entries
input string          InpSkipHoursUTC              = "21,22"; // Skip trading on these UTC hours (comma-separated, e.g., "21,22,23,0")
input double          InpBreakevenRR               = 1.0;    // Move SL to BE after reaching this RR
input bool            InpAllowTrailing             = true;   // Enable trailing SL

//========================
// Internal state & handles
//========================
int     hFastEMA = INVALID_HANDLE;
int     hSlowEMA = INVALID_HANDLE;
int     hRSI     = INVALID_HANDLE;
int     hATR     = INVALID_HANDLE;

datetime lastClosedBarTime = 0;

// Symbol parameters cache
string  gSymbol    = "";
double  gPoint     = 0.0;
int     gDigits    = 0;
double  gTickSize  = 0.0;
double  gTickValue = 0.0;
double  gMinVolume = 0.0;
double  gMaxVolume = 0.0;
double  gVolStep   = 0.0;
int     gStopsLevelPoints = 0;

//----------------------------
// Utility: Logging helpers
//----------------------------
void LogError(string where, string msg="")
{
   int err = _LastError;
   PrintFormat("[ERROR] %s failed (err=%d) %s", where, err, msg);
   ResetLastError();
}

void Info(string msg)
{
   PrintFormat("[INFO] %s", msg);
}

//----------------------------
// Utility: Symbol environment
//----------------------------
bool RefreshSymbolInfo()
{
   gSymbol = _Symbol;
   if(!SymbolInfoInteger(gSymbol, SYMBOL_SELECT))
      SymbolSelect(gSymbol, true);

   gPoint = SymbolInfoDouble(gSymbol, SYMBOL_POINT);
   gDigits = (int)SymbolInfoInteger(gSymbol, SYMBOL_DIGITS);
   gTickSize = SymbolInfoDouble(gSymbol, SYMBOL_TRADE_TICK_SIZE);
   gTickValue = SymbolInfoDouble(gSymbol, SYMBOL_TRADE_TICK_VALUE);
   gMinVolume = SymbolInfoDouble(gSymbol, SYMBOL_VOLUME_MIN);
   gMaxVolume = SymbolInfoDouble(gSymbol, SYMBOL_VOLUME_MAX);
   gVolStep   = SymbolInfoDouble(gSymbol, SYMBOL_VOLUME_STEP);
   gStopsLevelPoints = (int)SymbolInfoInteger(gSymbol, SYMBOL_TRADE_STOPS_LEVEL);

   if(gPoint <= 0 || gTickSize <= 0 || gMinVolume <= 0 || gVolStep <= 0)
   {
      LogError("RefreshSymbolInfo", StringFormat("Invalid symbol params: point=%.10f tick=%.10f volMin=%.2f step=%.2f", gPoint, gTickSize, gMinVolume, gVolStep));
      return false;
   }
   return true;
}

//----------------------------
// Indicator creation & data
//----------------------------
bool CreateIndicators()
{
   if(hFastEMA != INVALID_HANDLE) IndicatorRelease(hFastEMA);
   if(hSlowEMA != INVALID_HANDLE) IndicatorRelease(hSlowEMA);
   if(hRSI     != INVALID_HANDLE) IndicatorRelease(hRSI);
   if(hATR     != INVALID_HANDLE) IndicatorRelease(hATR);

   hFastEMA = iMA(gSymbol, InpTimeframe, InpFastEMA, 0, MODE_EMA, PRICE_CLOSE);
   if(hFastEMA == INVALID_HANDLE){ LogError("iMA(fast)"); return false; }

   hSlowEMA = iMA(gSymbol, InpTimeframe, InpSlowEMA, 0, MODE_EMA, PRICE_CLOSE);
   if(hSlowEMA == INVALID_HANDLE){ LogError("iMA(slow)"); return false; }

   hRSI = iRSI(gSymbol, InpTimeframe, InpRSIPeriod, PRICE_CLOSE);
   if(hRSI == INVALID_HANDLE){ LogError("iRSI"); return false; }

   hATR = iATR(gSymbol, InpTimeframe, InpATRPeriod);
   if(hATR == INVALID_HANDLE){ LogError("iATR"); return false; }

   // Ensure indicators are primed
   if(!BarsCalculated(hFastEMA) || !BarsCalculated(hSlowEMA) || !BarsCalculated(hRSI) || !BarsCalculated(hATR))
   {
      Print("[WARN] Indicators not yet calculated; waiting for data...");
   }
   return true;
}

bool GetIndicatorValues(double &fastPrev, double &fastCurr, double &slowPrev, double &slowCurr, double &rsiCurr, double &atrCurr)
{
   fastPrev = fastCurr = slowPrev = slowCurr = rsiCurr = atrCurr = 0.0;

   MqlRates rates[];
   if(CopyRates(gSymbol, InpTimeframe, 0, 3, rates) < 3) { LogError("CopyRates"); return false; }

   int startIndex = 0; // index 0=current forming bar, 1=last closed, 2=prev closed

   double bufFast[]; ArraySetAsSeries(bufFast, true);
   if(CopyBuffer(hFastEMA, 0, 0, 3, bufFast) < 3) { LogError("CopyBuffer fast"); return false; }

   double bufSlow[]; ArraySetAsSeries(bufSlow, true);
   if(CopyBuffer(hSlowEMA, 0, 0, 3, bufSlow) < 3) { LogError("CopyBuffer slow"); return false; }

   double bufRSI[]; ArraySetAsSeries(bufRSI, true);
   if(CopyBuffer(hRSI, 0, 0, 2, bufRSI) < 2) { LogError("CopyBuffer rsi"); return false; }

   double bufATR[]; ArraySetAsSeries(bufATR, true);
   if(CopyBuffer(hATR, 0, 0, 2, bufATR) < 2) { LogError("CopyBuffer atr"); return false; }

   // Use closed bars: index 1 = last closed, 2 = previous closed
   fastCurr = bufFast[1];
   fastPrev = bufFast[2];
   slowCurr = bufSlow[1];
   slowPrev = bufSlow[2];
   rsiCurr  = bufRSI[1];
   atrCurr  = bufATR[1];

   // ATR minimum movement filter
   if(InpATR_MinFilter > 0.0 && atrCurr < InpATR_MinFilter)
      return false;

   return true;
}

//----------------------------
// Filters: spread and session
//----------------------------
bool IsSpreadOK()
{
   MqlTick tick; if(!SymbolInfoTick(gSymbol, tick)) { LogError("SymbolInfoTick"); return false; }
   double spreadPoints = (tick.ask - tick.bid) / gPoint;
   return (spreadPoints <= InpMaxSpreadPoints);
}

bool IsHourBlocked(int utcHour)
{
   // Parse comma-separated list into matches
   string parts[]; int n = StringSplit(InpSkipHoursUTC, ',', parts);
   for(int i=0;i<n;i++)
   {
      string s = StringTrim(parts[i]);
      if(s == "") continue;
      int h = (int)StringToInteger(s);
      if(h == utcHour) return true;
   }
   return false;
}

bool IsSessionOK()
{
   datetime now = TimeCurrent();
   MqlDateTime dt; TimeToStruct(now, dt);
   if(IsHourBlocked(dt.hour))
      return false;
   return true;
}

//----------------------------
// Position utilities
//----------------------------
int CountOpenPositions()
{
   int count = 0;
   for(int i=0;i<PositionsTotal();i++)
   {
      ulong ticket = PositionGetTicket(i);
      if(ticket == 0) continue;
      if(!PositionSelectByTicket(ticket)) continue;
      if(PositionGetString(POSITION_SYMBOL) == gSymbol && (ulong)PositionGetInteger(POSITION_MAGIC) == InpMagicNumber)
         count++;
   }
   return count;
}

//----------------------------
// Risk & margin sizing
//----------------------------
double NormalizeVolume(double lots)
{
   if(lots < gMinVolume) lots = gMinVolume;
   if(lots > gMaxVolume) lots = gMaxVolume;
   // snap to step
   double steps = MathFloor(lots / gVolStep + 1e-8);
   double snapped = steps * gVolStep;
   // avoid zero due to rounding
   if(snapped < gMinVolume) snapped = gMinVolume;
   return snapped;
}

double CalcSLDistancePoints(ENUM_ORDER_TYPE type, double atr)
{
   double dist = MathMax(atr * InpATR_SL_Mult, gStopsLevelPoints * gPoint) / gPoint; // in points
   return MathMax((int)MathRound(dist), gStopsLevelPoints);
}

double CalcPriceSL(ENUM_ORDER_TYPE type, double entryPrice, double slPoints)
{
   if(type == ORDER_TYPE_BUY)
      return entryPrice - slPoints * gPoint;
   else
      return entryPrice + slPoints * gPoint;
}

double CalcPriceTP(ENUM_ORDER_TYPE type, double entryPrice, double slPoints)
{
   double tpPoints = slPoints * InpRR;
   if(type == ORDER_TYPE_BUY)
      return entryPrice + tpPoints * gPoint;
   else
      return entryPrice - tpPoints * gPoint;
}

bool CheckMarginLevelOK()
{
   double margin = AccountInfoDouble(ACCOUNT_MARGIN);
   double equity = AccountInfoDouble(ACCOUNT_EQUITY);
   double marginLevel = 0.0;
   if(margin > 0.0) marginLevel = equity / margin * 100.0;
   if(InpMinMarginLevelPct <= 0.0) return true; // disabled
   if(margin == 0.0) return true; // brokers may report 0 when flat; treat as OK
   return (marginLevel >= InpMinMarginLevelPct);
}

bool ComputePositionSize(ENUM_ORDER_TYPE type, double entryPrice, double slPoints, double &outLots, string &whyNot)
{
   outLots = 0.0; whyNot = "";

   // Current account context
   double equity      = AccountInfoDouble(ACCOUNT_EQUITY);
   double freeMargin  = AccountInfoDouble(ACCOUNT_FREEMARGIN);
   double contractSize= SymbolInfoDouble(gSymbol, SYMBOL_TRADE_CONTRACT_SIZE);

   if(equity <= 0.0) { whyNot = "Invalid equity"; return false; }
   if(freeMargin <= 0.0) { whyNot = "No free margin"; return false; }
   if(contractSize <= 0.0) { whyNot = "Invalid contract size"; return false; }

   // Risk in currency per 1.0 lot for given SL distance
   double riskPerLot = (slPoints * gPoint / gTickSize) * gTickValue;
   if(riskPerLot <= 0.0) { whyNot = "Invalid riskPerLot"; return false; }

   // Target risk amount
   double riskAmt = equity * (InpRiskPerTradePct / 100.0);
   if(riskAmt <= 0.0) { whyNot = "Risk amount is zero"; return false; }

   double rawLots = riskAmt / riskPerLot;
   if(rawLots <= 0.0) { whyNot = "Computed lots <= 0"; return false; }

   // Cap by free-margin usage using OrderCalcMargin
   double dev = InpSlippagePoints * gPoint;
   ENUM_ORDER_TYPE_FUTURE calcType = (type == ORDER_TYPE_BUY) ? ORDER_TYPE_BUY : ORDER_TYPE_SELL;

   double allowedLotsByFM = rawLots;
   // Iterate down until margin usage <= cap
   double maxMarginUse = freeMargin * (InpMaxFreeMarginUsagePct / 100.0);
   if(maxMarginUse > 0)
   {
      // Binary search-ish reduction
      double lo = gMinVolume, hi = MathMin(rawLots, gMaxVolume);
      double best = 0.0;
      for(int i=0;i<22;i++)
      {
         double mid = NormalizeDouble((lo + hi) * 0.5, 2);
         double price = 0.0; MqlTick t; if(SymbolInfoTick(gSymbol, t)) price = (type==ORDER_TYPE_BUY? t.ask : t.bid); else price = entryPrice;
         double needMargin = 0.0;
         if(!OrderCalcMargin(calcType, gSymbol, mid, price, needMargin))
         { LogError("OrderCalcMargin"); break; }
         if(needMargin <= maxMarginUse)
         { best = mid; lo = mid; }
         else hi = mid;
      }
      if(best > 0.0) allowedLotsByFM = MathMin(allowedLotsByFM, best);
   }

   double finalLots = NormalizeVolume(MathMin(rawLots, allowedLotsByFM));

   // Final feasibility checks
   if(finalLots < gMinVolume - 1e-8) { whyNot = "Lot size below minimum"; return false; }

   // Check margin level threshold after hypothetical add
   double price = 0.0; MqlTick tk; if(SymbolInfoTick(gSymbol, tk)) price = (type==ORDER_TYPE_BUY? tk.ask : tk.bid); else price = entryPrice;
   double addMargin = 0.0;
   if(!OrderCalcMargin(calcType, gSymbol, finalLots, price, addMargin))
   { LogError("OrderCalcMargin(final)"); return false; }

   // Simulate margin level if position added (approx):
   double curMargin = AccountInfoDouble(ACCOUNT_MARGIN);
   double curEquity = AccountInfoDouble(ACCOUNT_EQUITY);
   double newMargin = curMargin + addMargin;
   double newMarginLevel = (newMargin > 0.0 ? curEquity / newMargin * 100.0 : 0.0);
   if(InpMinMarginLevelPct > 0.0 && newMargin > 0.0 && newMarginLevel < InpMinMarginLevelPct)
   {
      whyNot = StringFormat("Margin level after entry would be %.1f%% < threshold %.1f%%", newMarginLevel, InpMinMarginLevelPct);
      return false;
   }

   // Ensure we don't exceed free margin
   if(addMargin > freeMargin)
   {
      whyNot = "Insufficient free margin for computed lot size";
      return false;
   }

   outLots = finalLots;
   return true;
}

//----------------------------
// Entry signals (new bar)
//----------------------------
int CheckSignal()
{
   // Returns: 1=buy, -1=sell, 0=none
   double fPrev,fCur,sPrev,sCur,rsi,atr; if(!GetIndicatorValues(fPrev,fCur,sPrev,sCur,rsi,atr)) return 0;

   bool emaBullNow = (fCur > sCur);
   bool emaBullPrev= (fPrev <= sPrev);
   bool emaBearNow = (fCur < sCur);
   bool emaBearPrev= (fPrev >= sPrev);

   if(emaBullNow && emaBullPrev && rsi >= InpRSI_Buy) return 1;
   if(emaBearNow && emaBearPrev && rsi <= InpRSI_Sell) return -1;
   return 0;
}

//----------------------------
// Order placement
//----------------------------
bool PlaceOrder(int dir)
{
   MqlTick tick; if(!SymbolInfoTick(gSymbol, tick)) { LogError("SymbolInfoTick"); return false; }

   ENUM_ORDER_TYPE type = (dir > 0 ? ORDER_TYPE_BUY : ORDER_TYPE_SELL);
   double price = (dir > 0 ? tick.ask : tick.bid);

   // Compute SL/TP
   double fPrev,fCur,sPrev,sCur,rsi,atr; if(!GetIndicatorValues(fPrev,fCur,sPrev,sCur,rsi,atr)) { return false; }
   double slPoints = CalcSLDistancePoints(type, atr);
   double slPrice  = CalcPriceSL(type, price, slPoints);
   double tpPrice  = CalcPriceTP(type, price, slPoints);

   // Stops level check
   double minStop = gStopsLevelPoints * gPoint;
   if(type == ORDER_TYPE_BUY)
   {
      if(price - slPrice < minStop) slPrice = price - minStop;
      if(tpPrice - price < minStop) tpPrice = price + minStop;
   }
   else
   {
      if(slPrice - price < minStop) slPrice = price + minStop;
      if(price - tpPrice < minStop) tpPrice = price - minStop;
   }

   // Risk & margin
   string why; double lots = 0.0;
   if(!CheckMarginLevelOK()) { Info("Blocked: margin level below threshold"); return false; }
   if(!ComputePositionSize(type, price, slPoints, lots, why)) { Info(StringFormat("Size calc blocked: %s", why)); return false; }

   trade.SetDeviationInPoints(InpSlippagePoints);
   trade.SetMagic(InpMagicNumber);

   bool ok = false;
   if(dir > 0)
      ok = trade.Buy(lots, gSymbol, price, slPrice, tpPrice, "EMA/RSI/ATR BUY");
   else
      ok = trade.Sell(lots, gSymbol, price, slPrice, tpPrice, "EMA/RSI/ATR SELL");

   if(!ok)
   {
      LogError("OrderSend", StringFormat("type=%s lots=%.2f price=%.5f sl=%.5f tp=%.5f", (dir>0?"BUY":"SELL"), lots, price, slPrice, tpPrice));
      return false;
   }
   else
   {
      Info(StringFormat("Order placed %s lots=%.2f price=%.5f sl=%.5f tp=%.5f", (dir>0?"BUY":"SELL"), lots, price, slPrice, tpPrice));
   }
   return true;
}

//----------------------------
// Trade management: BE & Trailing
//----------------------------
void ManageOpenPosition()
{
   if(CountOpenPositions() == 0) return;
   if(!PositionSelect(gSymbol)) return;
   if((ulong)PositionGetInteger(POSITION_MAGIC) != InpMagicNumber) return;

   long    type    = PositionGetInteger(POSITION_TYPE);
   double  price   = PositionGetDouble(POSITION_PRICE_OPEN);
   double  volume  = PositionGetDouble(POSITION_VOLUME);
   double  sl      = PositionGetDouble(POSITION_SL);
   double  tp      = PositionGetDouble(POSITION_TP);
   double  curBid  = SymbolInfoDouble(gSymbol, SYMBOL_BID);
   double  curAsk  = SymbolInfoDouble(gSymbol, SYMBOL_ASK);

   // Determine SL distance in points from current price
   double fPrev,fCur,sPrev,sCur,rsi,atr; if(!GetIndicatorValues(fPrev,fCur,sPrev,sCur,rsi,atr)) return;
   double trailPoints = MathMax((int)MathRound((atr * InpATR_TrailMult)/gPoint), gStopsLevelPoints);

   // Move to BE at InpBreakevenRR
   double entrySLPoints = 0.0;
   if(type == POSITION_TYPE_BUY)
      entrySLPoints = (price - sl) / gPoint;
   else
      entrySLPoints = (sl - price) / gPoint;

   double beTriggerMove = entrySLPoints * InpBreakevenRR * gPoint;

   if(type == POSITION_TYPE_BUY)
   {
      // Breakeven
      if(InpBreakevenRR > 0.0 && curBid - price >= beTriggerMove)
      {
         double newSL = MathMax(sl, price);
         if(newSL > sl + 0.1*gPoint)
            trade.PositionModify(gSymbol, newSL, tp);
      }
      // Trailing
      if(InpAllowTrailing)
      {
         double desiredSL = curBid - trailPoints * gPoint;
         if(desiredSL > sl + gPoint && curBid - desiredSL >= gStopsLevelPoints * gPoint)
            trade.PositionModify(gSymbol, desiredSL, tp);
      }
   }
   else if(type == POSITION_TYPE_SELL)
   {
      // Breakeven
      if(InpBreakevenRR > 0.0 && price - curAsk >= beTriggerMove)
      {
         double newSL = MathMin(sl, price);
         if(newSL < sl - 0.1*gPoint)
            trade.PositionModify(gSymbol, newSL, tp);
      }
      // Trailing
      if(InpAllowTrailing)
      {
         double desiredSL = curAsk + trailPoints * gPoint;
         if(desiredSL < sl - gPoint && desiredSL - curAsk >= gStopsLevelPoints * gPoint)
            trade.PositionModify(gSymbol, desiredSL, tp);
      }
   }
}

//----------------------------
// Standard events
//----------------------------
int OnInit()
{
   if(!RefreshSymbolInfo()) return(INIT_FAILED);
   if(!CreateIndicators()) return(INIT_FAILED);

   // Seed lastClosedBarTime
   MqlRates rates[];
   if(CopyRates(gSymbol, InpTimeframe, 0, 3, rates) >= 2)
      lastClosedBarTime = rates[1].time;
   else
      lastClosedBarTime = 0;

   Info("EA initialized");
   return(INIT_SUCCEEDED);
}

void OnDeinit(const int reason)
{
   if(hFastEMA != INVALID_HANDLE) IndicatorRelease(hFastEMA);
   if(hSlowEMA != INVALID_HANDLE) IndicatorRelease(hSlowEMA);
   if(hRSI     != INVALID_HANDLE) IndicatorRelease(hRSI);
   if(hATR     != INVALID_HANDLE) IndicatorRelease(hATR);
}

void OnTick()
{
   if(!RefreshSymbolInfo()) return;

   // Filters
   if(!IsSpreadOK()) return;
   if(!IsSessionOK()) return;

   // Enforce one-position-per-symbol
   int posCount = CountOpenPositions();

   // New bar detection
   MqlRates rates[];
   if(CopyRates(gSymbol, InpTimeframe, 0, 3, rates) < 2) return;
   datetime barTimeClosed = rates[1].time;
   bool isNewBar = (barTimeClosed != lastClosedBarTime);
   if(isNewBar) lastClosedBarTime = barTimeClosed;

   // Manage existing position every tick
   ManageOpenPosition();

   // Entry only on new closed bar and if flat
   if(!isNewBar || posCount > 0) return;

   int sig = CheckSignal();
   if(sig == 0) return;

   PlaceOrder(sig);
}

